# Code Structure And Maintainability

- Prefer decomposing code into smaller files and focused helpers whenever it clearly improves readability, reuse, or safety
- Do not keep growing a large file when a new section can live cleanly in a helper module
- Extract one concern per module when practical such as state helpers, visual helpers, AI helpers, export helpers, or statistical utilities
- Prefer pure functions for calculations and formatting helpers instead of mixing computation with UI state changes
- Centralize repeated state-reset or invalidation logic instead of copying similar blocks across files
- When refactoring, preserve existing behavior, widget keys, and user-facing flows unless the task explicitly asks for behavior changes
- Prefer small cohesive refactors over broad rewrites
- Add or keep brief comments only where the code would otherwise be hard to follow

Examples

```python
# bad
# giant app file mixes chart math, exports, state resets, and guide copy

# good
# app.py routes the workflow
# results_helpers.py handles chart math
# app_state.py handles reset helpers
# ui_content.py holds static guide content
```
